{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "hybrid",
  "name": "Hybrid XYA+C (A-tilt head on a CoreXY, C turntable)",
  "provenance": "docs/nonplanar/kinematics/hybrid (kinematics/kin.py HEAD_BOXES, cad/hybrid.scad). E3D V6 heatsink (diameter 22.3 x 26 mm, published drawing) at Z=26.5..52.5, V6 heater block 16 x 23 x 11.5 mm with a 1.5 mm silicone sock, long side along the A hinge (head X), at Z=12..23.5, a stock 20 mm M6 extended V6 nozzle: 7 mm hex at Z=9..12, 6 mm shank at Z=4.33..9, 60-degree included cone from the 1 mm land. A hinge axis at Z=30 along X: printed collar (radius 14, Z=23..37), two 6800 bearings in radius 12.5 housings to |X|=24 and the 24 mm Vectran capstan drum at X=25..36; these are cylinders about the hinge, so their boxes bound them at every A. Cooling outlets from a frame CPAP blower on both X sides at Z=7..12. The machine-fixed yoke arms and carriage are above the hinge and are not head boxes (kinematics/reach.py models them). Nozzle-tip frame +X right (hinge), +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Margins 0.3 mm. Dimensions from stock-part drawings, best estimate 2026-10-14; calibrated=false.",
